  "summary": "California AG Rob Bonta sued the City of El Cajon, alleging its police department violated state law by sharing ALPR data with law enforcement agencies in over two dozen out-of-state jurisdictions. The suit seeks a court declaration that the practice is unlawful and an order to stop. The article notes Gov. Newsom recently vetoed SB 274, which would have further regulated ALPR use.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "El Cajon has knowingly and repeatedly refused to comply with state law, jeopardizing the privacy and safety of individuals in its community.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "We're a sovereign city and we're acting within the law",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "El Cajon shared data with agencies in states including Texas, Florida, Georgia, Utah, Wisconsin, and Virginia",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
